        std = sqrt(sum((value - mean) ** 2 for value in values) / len(values))

        # A constant column has zero standard deviation, so map it to zeros.
        result[feature] = (
            [(value - mean) / std for value in values]
            if std != 0
            else [0.0] * len(values)
        )

    return result
```

This uses the population standard deviation. Constant feature columns are returned as zeros because they cannot have unit variance.

